////NEW REVIEW////
Went on to Youtube and watched some playthroughs/tutorials on this game.  Initially I was very frustrated (see below), but, after watching the walkthroughs, I have a better understanding/respect as to how this game is played and, indeed, how clever it is.  I've began playing it again and am enjoying it very much.  That said, I would like to see more opportunities/means to acquire resources and incentive for playing rather than waiting.  The current means is by waiting, challenging other players or the AI, or, defending your base.  However the rewards through playing, initially, were around 7K for supplies and gas but, taper off to around 2K.  Overall though, this game is growing on me more and more.
////OLD REVIEW////
You'll play this game initially and think wow, awesome, and amazing.  However, as you try to build up your base, forces, and get your feet wet, you'll have a higher level player stomp you....  I'm not sure if some of the other players experienced this, but, I found during one base defense mission, that I threw my entire range of forces at one tank and it took little to no damage and all my infantry and tanks died quickly.  The emplacements offered nothing in terms of resistance as well, dying in one to two hits.  Must have been Rambo manning the tank....  Point being, attackers took little to no damage and were at 100% force strength when he took out my base.
Good idea/concept.  Once the developers work out the hacks, bugs, and players who cheat, it will be a good game.  For now, though, this game still is a ways off from being anywhere near balanced or playable.  Feel free to hit me up with any questions.  Cheers

I have a little over 100 games and I rarely thumbs down games (this is only the second time), because developing a game takes hard work, no matter how bad I feel said game is.
However, I feel the need to thumb down this game:
- Feels sluggish/laggy from the get-go, but it gets worse as you get deeper into it;
- Crashes/kicks you randomly to menu, which is especially frustrating without any form of saved game;
- Terrible design decision (non-hosts can now buy stuff using their share of pooled money);
- No UI improvements from previous version (The non-HD version), it's still the same bad UI where you have to move pointer all over the screen in hopes of getting anything done;
- Some of the new zombies can now hit diagonally, across barricades, and destroy turrets (bad if not by design, worse if by design);
- Less than a day after release, cheats are out there, meaning leaderboards will be soon be meaningless;
- Issues/Bugs in the previous version are still present in this HD version (I'm not going to describe them here, they are known to the developer being they were posted in the other forum);
- The game is harder and they've (re)balanced some weapon/ammo prices, neither of which really bothers me, but neither of which really impresses me either. Specifically, the Flamethrower and the Freeze gun do not seem very effective anymore, which reduces even more the list of useful guns.
For those still interested, it's not all bad:
- Improved graphics;
- New enemies & one new playable character/skin;
- Power-ups/Cash drop more frequently;
- Cash still laying on the floor is absorbed at the end of night/round;
- Barricades no longer hinder movement during building phase;
- Unity engine instead of XNA engine, which opens the door to, among others, workshop integration;
- Only $4 ($1 for previous owners);

